---
import Glow from '../components/Glow.astro'
import Frame from '../layouts/Frame.astro'
---

<Frame title="Weft, a small sync engine" page="main" hint="Hold the mouse down to pull the two copies apart. Let go and they merge.">
  <section class="home">
    <p class="ident">weft<span>a small sync engine, written to learn</span></p>

    <p class="caption mono" style="top:24%;left:56%" data-caption>
      <b>Clock</b><br />hybrid, so order holds<br />when wall clocks lie
    </p>
    <p class="caption mono" style="top:69%;left:24%" data-caption>
      <b>Text</b><br />two people can type<br />in the same spot
    </p>

    <Glow tag="h1" lines={['Offline on', 'every device,', 'and still in sync.']} />

    <p class="lede">
      I wanted to understand what apps like Linear or Figma do when you lose signal, so I wrote a sync engine from scratch.
      It's about five hundred lines, and the tests throw thousands of broken networks at it to check that every copy ends up
      the same.
    </p>
  </section>
</Frame>
